{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310673,"nonce":"1kk75TBPaWMjbwTcSnQbRDHSdE8=","title":"2026-09-19 batch (560-\u003e564+, XML now parses+prints): `++x` after a block was POSTFIX on the block; parameters incremented with ++ not ...","message":"Commits 84c057bf (560-\u003e565) and 30015d6b (-\u003e567). git-bug c8a8f85 6aa7827 1e66390 fe4ce72 74022dd 0105f60 be985be 5b8760a 0eba620 bd928b8 8ea9ffc (fixed); OPEN: bd7be74 (enum through Dynamic = null), c3b6c52 (bound closure of a runtime-mapped extern method, `{iterator: m.keys}`), c5ec8bc (**`?len:Int` typed Int not Null\u003cInt\u003e ⇒ passed 0 reads as null; `Std.parseInt(..) \u003e= 128` compares the BOX POINTER** — blocks TestXML.testCustomXmlParser; ABI-wide change, touches every param-hint site).\n\n**Parser.** Haxe's grammar (grammar.ml) does NOT call `expr_next` after a block, `if`, `for`, `while`, `switch`, `try` or function literal — so `switch{...}\\n++p` is two statements. Both parsers applied `++` to the switch value: every `while` ending with `switch/if` + separate `++i` looped forever (haxe.xml.Parser). `(e[3])++` and `this++` ARE valid (Issue3247, Int32.hx) — the first fix (Ident/Field/Index only) broke Int32.hx and the RD parser fell back to the legacy one, which then produced a broken Int64 (`Cannot access field 'ucompare'`). A legacy-parser fallback warning is a real regression signal.\n\n**Loops.** `find_modified_variables_in_expression` never marked the operand of `++`/`--`; a PARAMETER is loop-carried only when assigned, so `++p` in a while left p at the signature register.\n\n**Import order.** The cycle breaker picked the stuck file with fewest outstanding deps — a user module with `using StringTools` (nothing depends on it) won and was typed before StringTools: every extension call `indirect`, the local vanished. Victims must have a stuck DEPENDENT. `RAYZOR_IMPORT_GRAPH=1` shows `dep -\u003e dependents` and the order.\n\n**Typer.** (1) `pre_register_class_fields` made a Dynamic `Field` symbol; lowering made a SECOND `Variable` symbol — methods typed earlier (or on a RETRY pass over a cyclic file; the file was lowered 9 times) kept the Dynamic one → `escapes.exists` E0801. Reuse the pre-registered symbol. (2) `var x = null` / `var x;` stays Dynamic: now typed at the first plain assignment (`null_inferred`, Null\u003cT\u003e for scalars). Haxe monomorph semantics. (3) for-in over a class with `iterator():Iterator\u003cT\u003e`: element typed Dynamic (structural_element_type never read a CLASS's own method); `class_method_return_type`. (4) `Lambda.array({iterator: x.attributes})` returned `Array\u003cA\u003e` unsubstituted: `unify_type_args` now expands aliases (incl. typedef-pre-registered-as-Class via `resolve_type_alias` + `types_for_symbol`), Function/Anonymous/Class args; `bind_return_type_params` applied at StaticMethodCall sites. `RAYZOR_BIND_TRACE=1`.\n\n**MIR.** (1) `iterator():Iterator\u003cT\u003e` returns a HANDLE (iter_handle.rs), not a class: compiled-iterator() path now `lower_for_in_iter_handle_reg`; `iterator_class_of` must return None for protocol names. (2) Anonymous `{iterator: f}`/`{hasNext,next}` → `IterSource::AnonIterable/AnonIterator`, stepped by runtime `rayzor_anon_iterable_iterator`/`rayzor_iter_value_has_next/next` (runtime/src/iter_handle.rs reads closure fields, walks nested handles). (3) Method closure of a CROSS-MODULE method: `lower_method_reference` only looked in function_map; now external_function_map + signature from `external_function_param_types` + HIR return. (4) `catch (e:Dynamic)` binds `rayzor_exception_as_dynamic()` (boxes payload by thrown type id); uncaught class exception prints via TO_STRING_REGISTRY. (5) `Null\u003cString\u003e` into Dynamic boxes as String; `Null\u003cEnum/Class\u003e` stays RAW on purpose (enum round trip broken, bd7be74; boxing it broke Template `::else::`). (6) StringMap\u003cString\u003e.get raw bits → cast to string when V=String.\n\n**Array reads.** `a[i]` past `len` (or on an EMPTY array, null data ptr) FAULTED — `Xml.firstChild()` = `children[0]`. Now branchless clamp: `idx \u003cu len ? (data,idx) : (obj,0)` + select zero (8ea9ffc). `build_select` now records the result type (a typeless select dest = W0020 `Type not found for Cmp operand`). Watch CI benchmarks.\n\n**Optimizer.** `apply_sra` walked blocks ONCE in BFS order; a pred not yet visited (loop cond block feeding the post-loop read) got the undef baseline → field phi `[null, obj, obj]` → `b.items == null` after ANY handle loop; two `for (x in b)` loops faulted. Now a fixed point with stable phi/copy ids, Undef baselines at the ENTRY block (they were at the alloc position and a pre-alloc loop header phi referenced them: `Value not found ... phi incoming`). `RAYZOR_SRA_DEBUG=\u003cfn substring\u003e` dumps after each replacement.\n\n**How to apply:** when a stdlib class \"throws on the first entity\"/\"prints `\u003cfoo/\u003e`\", copy the stdlib file VERBATIM into the probe dir (needs `[project]`+`[build] class-paths=[\".\"]` rayzor.toml) and `trace(p)` per iteration; a loop counter stuck at 0 is a PARSE bug before it is a lowering bug. The XML file trio was also behind pinned upstream — sync (`nsubs`/`buf.length` fix) rather than debug our copy.\n\n- Index summary moved from MEMORY.md (2026-10-18): 2026-09-19 84c057bf+30015d6b (560-\u003e567, XML parses/prints; OPEN c5ec8bc `?x:Int` is Int not Null\u003cInt\u003e): `switch{}\\n++p` PARSED AS POSTFIX (Haxe: no expr_next after block/if/switch/loop/try; `(e[3])++`,`this++` valid); `++param` not loop-carried; toposort victim outside the cycle; pre-registered field symbol duplicated; SRA single-pass reaching defs → null after loops; `var x=null` typed at 1st assign; structural iterables via runtime steppers. A legacy-parser FALLBACK warning = regression.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_postfix_after_block_and_iterables_batch` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}